    <h2 class="title-calm">FRC Robotics Camp</h2>
    <p>Every year, Team 6220 hosts this training camp, in partnership with LAEF, designed to introduce you to the innovative and electrifying world of robotics. For the cost of $450, you have the invaluable opportunity to learn from our experienced mentors and students in a three-week robotics program. Each day will introduce a unique set of captivating, educational challenges as you gain hands-on experience fabricating a robot with other passionate learners. Students will have the chance to gain additional, specialized knowledge in computer-aided manufacturing, programming, or design.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>8th-12th grade students (2026-27 school year)</li>
      <li>July 6-24, Monday-Friday, 8:30 AM-12:30 PM</li>
      <li>Los Al High School, Room 760 (Robotics Room)</li>
      <li>$450 registration (three weeks)</li>
      <li>Absolutely no experience required</li>
    </ul>
    <a class="btn btn-black" href="https://app.thestudiodirector.com/laef4kids/portal.sd?page=Enroll&meth=enroll&sident=1711560621052&cident=1769796583939" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sign up now ↗</a>
    <p>(or go to <a href="https://laef4kids.org/clinicscamps/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://laef4kids.org/clinicscamps/</a> --&gt; "Register Now" --&gt; Find class named "<a href="https://app.thestudiodirector.com/laef4kids/portal.sd?page=Login&cident=1769796583939" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Robotics - Summer Camp: Incoming Grades 8th-12th</a>")</p>

    <h2 class="title-calm">LEGO Robotics Camp</h2>
    <p>In collaboration with LAEF, this camp gives elementary and middle school students a chance to develop fundamental engineering and teamwork skills. Students work together in small groups to construct their own LEGO Mindstorms robot. Students learn to adapt our team's competition-winning mindset to problem-solving, iterating on design challenges while never giving up. The week-long camp also features many fun activities to give your students a blast while building collaborative, interpersonal skills.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>July 6-24, Monday-Friday, 9 AM-12 PM</li>
      <li>Los Al High School, Room 760 (dropoff)</li>
      <li>$250 registration (one week)</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>Three one-week camps:</b></p>
    <ol>
      <li>July 6-10: Grades 3-5</li>
      <li>July 13-17: Grades 5-7</li>
      <li>July 20-24: Grades 5-7</li>
    </ol>
